&lt;p&gt;This Saturday, November 22, the Bend Firefighters will host their annual Moustache Bash &ndash; a fundraiser supporting the Bend Firefighter&rsquo;s Community Assistance Program. The fundraiser will take place from 5 p.m. to 9 p.m. at 10 Barrel Brewing &ndash; East (62950 NE 18&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; Street, Bend).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Community members are invited to dress up as their favorite action hero and join in on the fun while supporting a good cause.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bash-goers will have opportunities to win prizes throughout the evening. Activities include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Costume Contest -&lt;/strong&gt; This year&rsquo;s theme is action heroes &lt;span style="font-family:arial,sans-serif"&gt;&ndash;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;suit up and have a chance to win!&lt;/li&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Moustache Contest -&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Featuring categories for everyone &ndash; including fake moustaches.&lt;/li&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raffle &ndash;&lt;/strong&gt; Raffle tickets are available for purchase. Enter to win one of many prizes donated by local businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Bend Firefighter&rsquo;s Community Assistance Program is a nonprofit started by Bend firefighters to help meet identified needs and respond to crises in the Bend community. Firefighters often encounter difficult situations where families require help beyond traditional fire department services.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Learn more about the Bend Fire Community Assistance Program or donate today at bendcommunityassistance.org.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

